{"id":526,"name":"gigalith","speciesId":526,"dex":526,"form":"normal","generation":5,"types":["rock"],"stats":{"hp":85,"attack":135,"defense":130,"special-attack":60,"special-defense":80,"speed":25},"abilities":[{"name":"sturdy","hidden":false},{"name":"sand-stream","hidden":false},{"name":"sand-force","hidden":true}],"height":17,"weight":2600,"baseExp":232,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/526.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/526.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/526.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/526.ogg","genus":"Compressed Pokémon","flavor":[{"version":"black","text":"Compressing the energy from its internal core lets it fire off an attack capable of blowing away a mountain."},{"version":"white","text":"The solar energy absorbed by its body’s orange crystals is magnified internally and fired from its mouth."},{"version":"black-2","text":"The solar rays it absorbs are processed in its energy core and fired as a ball of light."},{"version":"sun","text":"The blasts of energy it makes from sunbeams have terrifying power. However, it’s not able to fire its blasts at night or on rainy days."},{"version":"moon","text":"Known for its hefty horsepower, this Pokémon is a popular partner for construction workers."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"When it fires off energy with all its might, the power creates countless fissures on its body."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"It absorbs rays of sunlight and shoots out energy. It’s usually lurking deep beneath the surface."},{"version":"sword","text":"This hardy Pokémon can often be found on construction sites and in mines, working alongside people and Copperajah."},{"version":"shield","text":"Although its energy blasts can blow away a dump truck, they have a